WEBVTT

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:03.270
Audit events must never be deleted,

00:00:03.270 --> 00:00:04.110
so write it down.

00:00:04.500 --> 00:00:06.160
Audit Event is a resource,

00:00:06.330 --> 00:00:09.180
and its Append Only trait forbids hard delete,

00:00:09.300 --> 00:00:12.230
truncate and drop storage, for good.

00:00:12.830 --> 00:00:14.670
Audit Store owns the events,

00:00:14.860 --> 00:00:16.840
and grants what its functions may do.

00:00:16.840 --> 00:00:19.480
Each function states exactly what it does,

00:00:19.480 --> 00:00:20.720
and points to the code.

00:00:20.730 --> 00:00:22.000
The check passes.

00:00:22.600 --> 00:00:24.890
Now a pull request adds a purge

00:00:24.930 --> 00:00:27.070
job that claims a hard delete.

00:00:27.070 --> 00:00:29.310
The check fails with a forbidden effect,

00:00:29.310 --> 00:00:30.650
traced back to the trait.

00:00:31.300 --> 00:00:33.850
Granting the effect changes nothing:

00:00:33.850 --> 00:00:36.250
no grant overrides a final forbid.

00:00:36.920 --> 00:00:39.320
Every function gets two more checks.

00:00:39.430 --> 00:00:42.230
An effect the component never granted fails.

00:00:42.230 --> 00:00:44.660
And effects unknown fails too:

00:00:44.670 --> 00:00:46.430
a gap in the analysis

00:00:46.430 --> 00:00:48.130
never passes as no effects.

00:00:48.730 --> 00:00:51.450
Shape checks the claims against each other,

00:00:51.450 --> 00:00:53.080
not against your code.

00:00:53.320 --> 00:00:55.260
Reviewers follow the source links to confirm them.
